{
  "_comment": [
    "Candidate libre fonts for the X6200 GUI (issue #9, decision 1: migrate off the",
    "proprietary Sony/Arial families). The .c families under src/fonts/ are generated",
    "from these sources by tools/fonts/fonts.py and committed; the font binaries",
    "themselves are NOT vendored (they are downloaded into tools/fonts/.cache/, which is",
    "gitignored) so the repository keeps only the licence trace (docs/THIRD_PARTY.md).",
    "google_fonts_commit pins the revision every Google Fonts URL points at: a moving",
    "`main` would silently change the generated bytes.",
    "`stock` names the candidate generated into the ROM's own family slot (src/fonts/sony_*.c) and therefore the default the ROM draws with; flipping it is one line here plus `fonts.py generate`.",
    "`segmented_slots` are the slots the digit panels draw with (the frequency row's own labels are freq_main_style=sony_38 and freq_style=sony_30, src/styles.c, and the clock draws with sony_44 since issue #285 -- the three sizes the digit labels can name, src/clock.c). The candidates marked `segmented` are seven-segment LCD digit fonts: they are never a whole-family choice (the buttons and every label are letters), only the family of the digit labels via the theme's `font_digits` key. They are generated for those slots only, with `match: ink` (a segment digit is nearly as tall as its line height, so matching the line height would clip it) and with the stock family as their LVGL fallback."
  ],
  "google_fonts_commit": "94301472b4d809299b4775bc6502592b83dd6934",
  "stock": "firasans",
